
== 1. the verifier never signs, re-signs or writes a ref ==
  ok   no signing or ref-writing verb in verify_gitsign.py, by AST over its own subprocess argv
  ok   it fetches refs/tags read-only into a bare cache and reads the tag object

== 2. the pins are release.yml's, not literals ==
  ok   identity regexp matches release.yml: ^https://github\.com/policy-as-versioned-platform/platform/\.github/workflows/cut-release\.yml@refs/heads/(main|release/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.x)$
  ok   issuer matches release.yml: https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com

== 3. the fixture is this repo's own signed tag, byte for byte ==
  ok   fixture == git cat-file tag policy/v3.0.0 (3642 bytes)

== 4. it ACCEPTS the real signed tag under the release.yml pins ==
  VERIFIED: signed by https://github.com/policy-as-versioned-platform/platform/.github/workflows/cut-release.yml@refs/heads/main (issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com) at 1787475175

== 4b. the trust instant: a certificate issued AFTER the tagger time, within the declared bound ==
  ok   deployment.yaml declares GITSIGN_TAGGER_SKEW_SECONDS=60
  ok   fixture: certificate notBefore is 1s after the tagger time, the race the verifier must survive
  VERIFIED: signed by https://github.com/policy-as-versioned-driftwood/driftwood/.github/workflows/cut-release.yml@refs/heads/main (issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com) at 1787677714 (certificate issued 1s later; chained at 1787677715)
  ok   accepted at the later instant, both instants reported
  ok   rejected when the gap exceeds the bound, naming the gap and the knob
         certificate notBefore is 1s after the tagger time 1787677714, over the declared tolerance of 0s (GITSIGN_TAGGER_SKEW_SECONDS); the tag claims to predate the certificate that signs it by more than the bound allows
  ok   rejected a tampered racy payload under the same bound
  ok   gitsign verify-tag agrees: the racy tag is good under the same pins

== 5. it REJECTS everything that is not that ==
  ok   rejected a tampered payload
         signature did not verify over the tag payload: 804B2CF26A7F0000:error:1700006D:CMS routines:CMS_verify:content verify error:../crypto/cms/cms_smime.c:457:
  ok   rejected a tampered signature
         signature carries no signer certificate (openssl pkcs7: 808B3E8AD17F0000:error:0688010A:asn1 encoding routines:asn1_template_ex_d2i:nested asn1 error:../crypto/asn1/tasn_dec.c:537:Field=d.sign, Type=PKCS7)
  ok   rejected a self-signed forgery wearing the right identity, by the chain not the bound
         certificate chain did not verify at 1788572372 (tagger time 1787475175, certificate notBefore 1788572372): error /tmp/tmp3yxb_xho/leaf.pem: verification failed
  ok   rejected a wrong identity
         signer identity 'https://github.com/policy-as-versioned-platform/platform/.github/workflows/cut-release.yml@refs/heads/main' does not match the pinned regexp '^https://github\\.com/policy-as-versioned-ico/ico/.*$'
  ok   rejected a wrong issuer
         signer issuer 'https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com' is not the pinned issuer 'https://accounts.google.com'
  ok   rejected an unanchored identity regexp
         the pinned identity regexp '.*' is not anchored at both ends; an unanchored pattern matches a substring of any identity and pins nothing
  ok   rejected an identity regexp anchored at one end only
         the pinned identity regexp '^https://github\\.com/' is not anchored at both ends; an unanchored pattern matches a substring of any identity and pins nothing

== 6. differential against gitsign itself ==
  ok   gitsign verify-tag agrees: policy/v3.0.0 is good under the same pins

== 7. the controller's verdict reaches the objects it is supposed to gate ==
  ok   trust_instant: later-of within the bound, refused past it, a bad declaration is could-not-look
  ok   verified source: annotates gitsign-verified=true, leaves the gate alone
  ok   racy source: verified under the declared bound, reason carries both instants
  gate flux-system/platform-policy: SUSPENDED -- v1.1.0: certificate notBefore is 1s after the tagger time 1787677714, over the declared tolerance of 0s (GITSIGN_TAGGER_SKEW_SECONDS); the tag claims to predate the certificate that signs it by more than the bound allows
  ok   racy source with no bound declared: rejected, gate suspended, reason names the knob
  gate flux-system/platform-policy: left as it is -- could not look at v1.1.0: GITSIGN_TAGGER_SKEW_SECONDS='sixty' is not a whole number of seconds
  ok   a mis-declared tolerance: records unknown and moves no gate
  gate flux-system/platform-policy: SUSPENDED -- policy/v3.0.0: signature did not verify over the tag payload: 804BB727307F0000:error:1700006D:CMS routines:CMS_verify:content verify error:../crypto/cms/cms_smime.c:457:
  ok   rejected source: suspends flux-system/platform-policy and marks it its own
  gate flux-system/platform-policy: released -- policy/v3.0.0 signed by https://github.com/policy-as-versioned-platform/platform/.github/workflows/cut-release.yml@refs/heads/main at 1787475175
  ok   released: a gate this controller suspended is released when the tag verifies again
  ok   a suspend the controller did not take is left alone
  gate flux-system/platform-policy: left as it is -- could not fetch policy/v3.0.0: Command '['git', 'fetch']' returned non-zero exit status 128.
  ok   could not look: records unknown, never true, and moves no gate either way

